From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:04:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posture: report laptop/slate to Windows and add handheld full
 screen mode

A reported small monitor docks the touch keyboard, but Windows only switches
to tablet behaviour (touch keyboard on text focus, tablet taskbar) when it
believes the machine is a convertible with the keyboard folded back or
detached. A virtual display host is neither, so while a touch-primary client
streams the host reports the state itself through the Windows laptop/slate
indicator interface, and reports laptop again a few seconds after the last
touch client left (so a resume does not flicker the shell).

- src/tablet_posture.*, tablet_posture_policy.h: client registry, state
  machine and worker thread; all Windows work runs off the streaming and HTTP
  threads; crash recovery at start, restore at shutdown;
- src/platform/windows/tablet_posture.cpp: the ROOT\HIDCLASS indicator device;
- handheld mode: a handheld client also asks for the Xbox full screen
  experience (gaming posture) via src/platform/windows/gaming_posture.cpp,
  switched by a short-lived helper instance of the host started as the
  logged-on user (--gaming-posture-switch, handled first in main());
- stream session start/end register and release the client, main() runs
  recovery and shutdown;
- /api/tablet-posture (GET status, POST simulate slate/laptop/handheld/auto);
- installer: the MSI removes only the indicator node it created on uninstall.

The Xbox full screen part is inseparable from the registry in the same files,
so both live in this patch. Unit tests cover the pure policy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
